# Line endings, pinned where they are load-bearing.
#
# `core.autocrlf = true` on Windows rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. For most of the
# repo that is harmless. For these it is not: the overlay page is read with `include_str!` and the
# contract tests match text inside it, so the same commit has to produce the same bytes on a Windows
# checkout and a macOS one.
#
# Pinning LF here means the tests are testing the file, not the machine that checked it out.

src-tauri/src/overlay/** text eol=lf
tools/** text eol=lf
